From 77b4fef5127cc0a00a826e61872d872e18a594d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:59:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v6] mm: batch file VMA insertions in dup_mmap

dup_mmap() acquires i_mmap_rwsem separately for each file VMA copied
into the child mm. Dynamically linked binaries commonly have several
mappings of each shared library, repeatedly acquiring the same lock to
insert those VMAs into the file's reverse mapping tree.

Batch up to eight insertions for the same address_space under one
i_mmap write lock, following the unlink batching introduced by commit
3577dbb19241 ("mm: batch unlink_file_vma calls in free_pgd_range").
Group by address_space so mappings through different file instances can
share a batch. Reuse the counted VMA array from unlink batching and keep
the corresponding source VMAs needed to insert each child after its
parent.

Flush pending insertions before copying a file VMA's page tables, so
concurrent reverse mapping walks can find the child mapping. Share
vma_needs_copy() with copy_page_range() to identify this boundary while
allowing VMAs that need no page table copy to remain queued. Drain the
remaining batch on both successful and failed exits from the loop,
before tearing down a failed fork.

Tracing batch sizes on 2026-11-24, before this rebase, during a partial
kernel build (-j2, kernel/fork.o, mm/mmap.o and mm/rmap.o) showed:

[1, 2)      563 |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|
[2, 3)        0 |                                                |
[3, 4)        0 |                                                |
[4, 5)      486 |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@       |

There were 486 opportunities to coalesce four lock acquisitions into
one. The 2507 file VMA insertions required 1049 lock acquisitions, a
58.16% reduction compared with acquiring the lock for each VMA. The
number of tree insertions is unchanged.

Stats were collected in an x86_64 QEMU KVM guest with KASAN and lockdep,
using tracefs kprobes to sample the batch count at entry to
link_file_vma_batch_process(). The count field was fetched with:

  p:mbatch/link_batch link_file_vma_batch_process count=+0($arg1):u32

The trace covers the build command and its descendants. Each batch
count was checked against actual tree insertions, with no lost events
or missed probes. Throughput has not been compared against an unpatched
kernel.

Prepared with LLM assistance, including OpenAI Codex for the rebase,
probe tests and commit message.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
 mm/internal.h | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 mm/memory.c   | 32 +--------------------
 mm/mmap.c     | 80 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 mm/vma.c      |  8 +++---
 mm/vma.h      | 12 ++++----
 5 files changed, 111 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/internal.h b/mm/internal.h
index 85cf7becf858..7bd7c8e2dd95 100644
--- a/mm/internal.h
+++ b/mm/internal.h
@@ -283,6 +283,36 @@ void unmap_vmas(struct mmu_gather *tlb, struct unmap_desc *unmap);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_MMU
 
+/*
+ * Return true if the vma needs to copy the pgtable during this fork().  Return
+ * false when we can speed up fork() by allowing lazy page faults later until
+ * when the child accesses the memory range.
+ */
+static inline bool
+vma_needs_copy(struct vm_area_struct *dst_vma, struct vm_area_struct *src_vma)
+{
+	/*
+	 * We check against dst_vma as while sane VMA flags will have been
+	 * copied, VM_UFFD_WP may be set only on dst_vma.
+	 */
+	if (dst_vma->vm_flags & VM_COPY_ON_FORK)
+		return true;
+	/*
+	 * The presence of an anon rmap indicates the VMA may map anonymous
+	 * folios which naturally cannot be reconstituted on page fault.
+	 */
+	if (vma_has_anon_rmap(src_vma))
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * Don't copy ptes where a page fault will fill them correctly.  Fork
+	 * becomes much lighter when there are big shared or private readonly
+	 * mappings. The tradeoff is that copy_page_range is more efficient
+	 * than faulting.
+	 */
+	return false;
+}
+
 bool cond_install_uffd_wp_ptes(struct vm_area_struct *vma,
 		unsigned long addr, pte_t *ptep, pte_t pte,
 		unsigned long nr_ptes);
